<BaseLayout title="Now"><section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16"><p class="eyebrow">From the desk</p><h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold text-ink">Now</h1><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate">A small record of what has my attention. It is allowed to be incomplete.</p><div class="now-list mt-12"><section><p class="eyebrow">Trying to get clearer on</p><h2>Detection systems that explain themselves</h2><p>An alert should say more than “something matched.” I’m interested in the context that lets an investigator tell whether a result is useful before opening five other tools.</p></section><section><p class="eyebrow">Returning to</p><h2>Old protocols with very current consequences</h2><p>DNS and Kerberos are good examples: familiar, durable, and easy to oversimplify when talking about risk.</p></section><section><p class="eyebrow">Still undecided</p><h2>What should a good security control feel like to operate?</h2><p>Probably useful, legible, and modest about what it can actually prove. That last part is harder than it sounds.</p></section></div><p class="mt-12 font-mono text-sm text-slate">Last refreshed: August 2026</p></section></BaseLayout>
